# title_caption_table.xlsx -- FROZEN EXPECTATION.
# A frozen expectation is corrected ONLY when the reading of the third-party-authored fixture was
# wrong -- never edited to chase an FSA1 regression.
#
# The `region:` lines are the SEMANTIC reading, written from the authored structure before `unpack`
# was run on this file. The `block:` lines are the hand-derivation below, executed on the fixture's
# own `s=` attributes.
#
# THE SIGNATURES, off xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml:
#   s="1" on A1,B1        the title line       (bold 14pt)   -- call it t
#   s="2" on A2,A3        the caption          (italic 9pt)  -- c
#   s="3" on A4,B4,C4     the header row       (bold 11pt)   -- h
#   s="4" on A5:C9        the body             (10pt)        -- b
# B2, C2, B3 and C3 are unoccupied and read None, the same value an unstated coordinate carries.
# Nothing here is blank-but-styled, so the occupancy and the stated cells are the same 22 coordinates.
#
# 1. SEED. Each signature's group is covered on its own, row-major and greedily. t is {A1,B1}: two
#    wide, one deep (row 2 holds no t) -> A1:B1. c is {A2,A3}: one wide (B2 is not in the group), two
#    deep -> A2:A3. h -> A4:C4. b -> A5:C9. Four regions, each gapless over ONE signature, so each
#    costs exactly one rule: the potential is 4 rules + 4 lambda = 8.
#
# 2. PASS 1, parity 0 -- the anchors with (col+row) even: A1:B1 and A5:C9.
#    A1:B1 down lands on row 2 and takes A2:B2, spanning its OWN two columns: B2 is unoccupied, which
#    suppresses the modal over the merged A1:B2, leaving one row rule for the title row and one
#    leftover for A2 -- 2 rules. It also cuts A2:A3 down to A3. Before 1+1+1+1 = 4, after 2+1 plus
#    A3's 1+1 = 5: gain -1, not a candidate. Column B is its right edge and columns C..E hold nothing
#    on row 1, so it reaches nothing sideways either.
#    A5:C9 up lands on row 4 and takes the whole header row, which no other region shares. The merged
#    A4:C9 is gapless: modal b, one row rule for the header -> 2 rules. Before 1+1+1+1 = 4, after
#    2+1 = 3: gain +1, the pass's only candidate, and it is applied. Regions: A1:B1, A2:A3, A4:C9.
#
# 3. PASS 2, parity 1: A2:A3 and A4:C9.
#    A2:A3 up takes A1 alone -- a region grows by whole strips of its OWN extent, one column here --
#    which cuts the title line down to B1. Before 4, after rules(A1:A3) = 2, +1, plus B1's 1+1 = 5:
#    gain -1. Down it takes A4 alone, cutting A4:C9 into B4:C9 and A5:A9: before 1+1+2+1 = 5, after
#    2+1 + 2+1 + 1+1 = 8: gain -3.
#    A4:C9 up takes A3:C3 across all three of its columns. B3 and C3 are unoccupied, so the merged
#    A3:C9 has no modal at all and every one of its six occupied rows needs a rule of its own, plus a
#    leftover for A3: 7 rules. Before 2+1 + 1+1 = 5, after 7+1 plus A2's 1+1 = 10: gain -5. Rows 10-12
#    and columns D-F are empty, so it reaches nothing down or right.
#    Nothing applied.
#
# 4. PASS 3, parity 0: A1:B1's one reachable move is the same -1 against a region set that has not
#    moved. A second silent pass, so growth stops. THREE blocks.
#
# 5. `--decompose occupancy` reads no signature: the sheet's 22 occupied cells sit in a 3x9 bounding
#    box, area 27, under the policy's 256-cell floor, so no cut pays and it writes ONE block A1:C9.
#    Of the three labelled starts -- rows 1, 2 and 4 -- it emits row 1 and misses two.
sheet:  Report
region: 1-1 the title line
region: 2-3 the caption
region: 4-9 the table, its bold header row and its five body rows
block:  A1:B1
block:  A2:A3
block:  A4:C9
policy: appearance
misses: 2
